# A diagram built to fail the label check, so the check itself is testable.
#
# The defect it reproduces: D2 centres a container's title on its top border,
# dagre routes an incoming edge into the top of that container, and the arrow
# is drawn through the text. The title is deliberately wide enough to occupy
# the middle, which is where the edge comes in.
#
# If tests/test_render.sh ever reports this file as clean, the checker has
# stopped checking — that happened twice while it was being written, once
# because a regex could not handle nested <g>, and once because an edge id
# arrives HTML-escaped so `-&gt;` never matched `->`. Both times it found
# nothing and said so cheerfully.

source: sender

target: "a container title wide enough to sit under the incoming edge" {
  inner: something
}

source -> target.inner
